{
 "encounter_id": "00866",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Um, hello. I've had diarrhoea, I'm sorry to say, for ten days now, since I got back from holiday. It's not stopping."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Where were you? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Egypt. A week in Hurghada. I was fine there, mostly, then it started on the flight home."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How often are you going?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Five or six times a day. Watery. And I've lost my appetite."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any tummy pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Cramping, before I go. Then it eases."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any blood, or mucus, in the stool?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. No blood. Just watery."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit hot, the first few days. Not now. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What are you taking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Omeprazole, 20 mg, once a day. And loperamide, I think, 2 mg, when I need to go out."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does the loperamide help? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit. For a few hours. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any other conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Acid reflux."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My gallbladder, in 2016."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did you eat anything unusual, salads, ice, or drink tap water? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ice in my drinks. And a buffet. I know, I know. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's the usual story. Let me press your tummy. Lie back.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your tummy is soft with mild general tenderness, and no guarding. Your mouth is slightly dry. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it serious? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Persistent traveller's diarrhoea after ten days, I'd say it's likely a gut infection picked up abroad, possibly a parasite like giardia, though bacteria are also possible."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What do I do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to send a stool sample, to look for bacteria and parasites."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please drink plenty of fluids with some salt and sugar, and eat plain food."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Don't take the loperamide if you get a fever or blood in the stool."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If you get blood, a high fever, severe pain, or can't keep fluids down, come back at once."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. Thanks. ~"
  }
 ],
